      "knowledge_id": "unirank-method-zenith",
      "decision": "considered",
      "rationale": "Retrieved card highlights separate ID capacity and a uniform-width control. Local measured parameter dominance supports first testing simple uniform/dense reductions; no observed per-field redundancy or authorized frequency diagnostics justify an ID-specific allocation yet. Original paper detail remains unverified.",
      "transformed_mechanism": "None adopted: no expanded ID tables, ID tokens or Zenith blocks.",
      "variant_names": [],
      "nearest_work_difference": "Our cells retain the source representation units and pooling and vary two widths; Zenith card describes separate ID and attribute paths. This is a limited descriptive distinction, not an originality claim.",
      "falsifier": "If E8 consistently loses quality, reconsider selective capacity retention only with field-frequency diagnostics and matched-total-parameter controls; the card alone does not predict local success.",
      "source_refs": [
        "unirank-benchmark-v2",
        "unirank-code:Zenith",
        "paper:zenith"
      ],
